{
  "cell": {
    "type": "hive"
  },
  "params": {
    "ports": [],
    "required_drains": [
      {
        "accepts": "turn",
        "emits": "answer",
        "because": "a turn nobody takes back leaves the caller waiting"
      },
      {
        "accepts": "tool_result",
        "emits": "answer",
        "because": "a client result continues the turn it belongs to"
      },
      {
        "accepts": "close",
        "emits": "close_report",
        "because": "the receipt says the close pass ran and the dream was triggered"
      },
      {
        "accepts": "in_model",
        "emits": "model_refused",
        "because": "a refused push is otherwise silent"
      },
      {
        "accepts": "in_pack",
        "emits": "pack_ack",
        "because": "the colony's affinity books a pack only on its receipt"
      },
      {
        "accepts": "in_conversations",
        "emits": "conversations",
        "because": "a reader that is never answered cannot tell an empty history from a lost answer"
      }
    ],
    "contract": {
      "accepts": [
        {
          "route": "turn",
          "because": "one turn of the caller: hop `turn_id`, `session_id`, `channel`, `audience_set`; body `messages` (meclaw turns, or `{role, content}`) and optional `tools[]` (provider schemas, `{name, description, parameters}` or the OpenAI `function` form). `tools[]` is the client's menu for THIS turn only; a turn without it empties that menu. A client tool named like one of the agent's own is dropped (hop `client_tools_dropped`)"
        },
        {
          "route": "tool_result",
          "because": "the result of one client call: `{id, content, is_error?}`; the hop brings back `turn_id`, `session_id`, `iter`, `channel`, `audience_set` exactly as the `calls` message carried them, or the result is refused as `tool_result_unkeyed`"
        },
        {
          "route": "close",
          "because": "the end of a session: `{session_id}`. The curator closes it, the memory reads it whole once (one model call) and the dream is triggered; `close_report` answers after the close pass"
        },
        {
          "route": "in_pack",
          "at": [
            "./curator"
          ],
          "required": true,
          "because": "the agent's identity and `instructions`, pushed by the colony's affinity to the subscription of the agent's entry (`slots: [\"identity\"]`), into the brain's system slots (`identity`, `persona`, `handover`, `instructions`) as the curator's pack lane takes them. A V-LANE docking at `./curator`, the one address this rim opens for it. The embedder's edge promotes `hop.pack_sub` and `hop.pack_hash` into context; the receipt leaves on `pack_ack` with both. Required: a birth without the edge is refused, the agent would never learn who it is"
        },
        {
          "route": "in_model",
          "because": "a model package for one model cell of this hive, pushed by the colony's llm-registry (GH #858). `hop.subscriber` names the cell; without one it goes to `./brain`. Required: the colony's llm-registry is the only way a model reaches the agent",
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "route": "in_sealed",
          "at": [
            "./brain",
            "./strong",
            "./curator/summarizer",
            "./memory-hive/closer",
            "./memory-hive/dialectic",
            "./memory-hive/dreamer",
            "./memory-hive/judge",
            "./memory-hive/embed",
            "./tools/web_search"
          ],
          "required": true,
          "because": "the answer half of the credential lane: the colony access's `ack` for `vault.deliver` with the sealed box, renamed at the boundary, addressed by `hop.grant_id` (one grant per consumer, set by the embedder at birth through `override_params`). It lands on the cell that asked and on nothing else -- the box is sealed to that cell's ephemeral key. Required: a model cell without it waits for a box nobody sends"
        },
        {
          "route": "in_briefing",
          "at": [
            "./collector"
          ],
          "required": true,
          "because": "the colony affinity's answer (or error, `hop.brief_outcome == 'error'`, stamped by the embedder) to this turn's `brief`, the third leg of the turn; a V-LANE docking at `./collector`, the one address this rim opens for it; an error parks the leg empty and the turn goes on without a brief. Required: with `brief_slots` set a turn with a counterpart waits for it"
        },
        {
          "route": "in_note",
          "at": [
            "./curator"
          ],
          "because": "notes for the window (curator C1, GH #1303) -- a care or role hint near the newest turn; the embedder's edge reaches the curator one level deeper"
        },
        {
          "route": "in_propose_ack",
          "because": "the colony affinity's `ack` (or `error`, `hop.propose_outcome == 'error'`, stamped by the embedder) of one `affinity_propose`, back into its round as the affinity tool's `tool_result`; anything but an accepted write reads `error:`, never silence; one that carries `context.sa_enrol` is the enrolment's own and goes to `./enrol`, which takes the next step"
        },
        {
          "route": "mutation_committed",
          "because": "the graph moved: the collector asks for its tools again, and `./enrol` writes the agent's entry, its disclosures and its subscriptions at the colony's affinity when the receipt is the agent's own: the boot's, every manifest's (it names no scope but `/`), or a single mutation whose scope is the agent, lies under it or is its level (idempotent; a single mutation elsewhere writes nothing)"
        },
        {
          "route": "in_conversations",
          "because": "the mandatory capability of every simple-agent@2 (R-SA-17 (3)): a reader asks this agent's memory for whole conversations; the lane lands on the agent's own memory hive (`in_conversations` there, its form unchanged) and the answer leaves on `conversations`"
        }
      ],
      "emits": [
        {
          "route": "answer",
          "because": "the turn's final answer: `{turn_id, text, partial?, stale?}` -- `partial` when the loop hit `max_iter`, `stale` when a client result never came and the turn went on without it"
        },
        {
          "route": "calls",
          "because": "one client call the brain made: body `calls {id, name, arguments}`; hop `turn_id`, `session_id`, `iter`, `channel`, `audience_set`, `tool_name`, `tool_call_id`. The caller answers it on `tool_result` with the same hop keys"
        },
        {
          "route": "close_report",
          "because": "the receipt of a `close`: `{session_id, ok, added, closed}` after the memory's close report (`ok` false when the close pass was refused)"
        },
        {
          "route": "credential_request",
          "at": [
            "./brain",
            "./strong",
            "./curator/summarizer",
            "./memory-hive/closer",
            "./memory-hive/dialectic",
            "./memory-hive/dreamer",
            "./memory-hive/judge",
            "./memory-hive/embed",
            "./tools/web_search"
          ],
          "because": "the ask half of the credential lane: a model cell born with a `credential_grant_id` and no key sends the grant handle with a fresh recipient key. A V-LANE: `ports` stays `[]` and the nine cells in `at` (the seven model cells and `./tools/web_search`) are the only addresses this rim opens for it; the embedder points the edge at the colony's access and stamps `context.requester` (R-AC-1). A cell nested in the memory hive or the curator names its full path, because every sealed level the edge crosses must open for it"
        },
        {
          "route": "pack_ack",
          "because": "the receipt of one pack that came in on `in_pack`, accepted and refused alike (`hop.error_code` empty, `slot_unknown` or `pack_empty`), with `context.pack_sub` and `context.pack_hash` as the embedder's edge promoted them, for the colony affinity's `in_pack_ack`. The door's own frame pack never leaves"
        },
        {
          "route": "brief",
          "because": "the brief about this turn's counterpart (GH #834): raised by the collector at the turn's opening when `brief_slots` is set and the turn names a `counterpart` -- one `tool_call` `{subject, channel, slots}`, `hop.turn_id` the turn, the round as `context.audience_set`. The embedder stamps the asker and carries it to the colony's affinity (`in_brief`), which refuses a brief without a round"
        },
        {
          "route": "affinity_propose",
          "because": "one write of the affinity tool into the agent's entry in the colony's affinity, as its `in_propose` takes it: a `tool_call` turn whose text is the op; hop `agent_id` (the embedder stamps the actor `agent:<agent_id>` from it, never from the body) and the round keys. The answer comes back on `in_propose_ack`; the enrolment's writes (`upsert_entity`, `set_disclosure`, `subscribe`) leave on the same lane with `context.sa_enrol` naming the step, and for `subscribe`/`subscribe_brain` the embedder's edge stamps the subscriber token"
        },
        {
          "route": "model_refused",
          "because": "a model package pushed through `in_model` that a model cell refused (GH #863)"
        },
        {
          "route": "error",
          "because": "a failed turn (`{error_code, turn_id}`), a refused rim message (`turn_without_id`, `tool_result_unkeyed`, `close_without_session`) or a refused frame pack (`kind: pack`); never silent; `enrol_refused` (`{error_code, step, reason_code}`) when the colony's affinity refused a step of the enrolment"
        },
        {
          "route": "conversations",
          "because": "the agent's memory hive's answer to `in_conversations`, to the reader named on `hop.reader`"
        }
      ]
    },
    "graph": {
      "edges": [
        {
          "from": ".",
          "to": "./door",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'turn' && !has(hop.sa_rim)"
        },
        {
          "from": ".",
          "to": "./door",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'tool_result' && !has(hop.sa_rim)"
        },
        {
          "from": ".",
          "to": "./door",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'close' && !has(hop.sa_rim)"
        },
        {
          "from": ".",
          "to": "./door",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_propose_ack' && !(has(context.sa_enrol) && context.sa_enrol != '')"
        },
        {
          "from": ".",
          "to": "./collector",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'mutation_committed'"
        },
        {
          "from": ".",
          "to": "./enrol",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'mutation_committed'"
        },
        {
          "from": ".",
          "to": "./enrol",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_propose_ack' && has(context.sa_enrol) && context.sa_enrol != ''"
        },
        {
          "from": "./enrol",
          "to": ".",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'affinity_propose' && has(hop.sa_rim) && hop.sa_rim == 'out'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_hop": {
              "route": "'affinity_propose'"
            },
            "set_context": {
              "sa_enrol": "hop.sa_enrol"
            },
            "delete_context": [
              "col_phase",
              "curator_call",
              "tool_answerer",
              "recall_input_soft",
              "input_soft",
              "gap_ask",
              "tools_folded",
              "sa_pack",
              "sa_kind",
              "pack_sub",
              "pack_hash",
              "agent_id",
              "tools_allow",
              "tools_deny",
              "tool_require",
              "ds_kind",
              "sa_stage"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./enrol",
          "to": ".",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'error' && has(hop.sa_rim) && hop.sa_rim == 'out'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_hop": {
              "route": "'error'"
            },
            "delete_context": [
              "col_phase",
              "curator_call",
              "tool_answerer",
              "recall_input_soft",
              "input_soft",
              "gap_ask",
              "tools_folded",
              "sa_pack",
              "sa_kind",
              "pack_sub",
              "pack_hash",
              "agent_id",
              "tools_allow",
              "tools_deny",
              "tool_require",
              "ds_kind",
              "sa_stage"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "from": ".",
          "to": "./brain",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_model' && !(has(hop.subscriber) && (hop.subscriber.endsWith('/strong') || hop.subscriber.endsWith('/curator/summarizer') || hop.subscriber.contains('/memory-hive/')))"
        },
        {
          "from": ".",
          "to": "./strong",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_model' && has(hop.subscriber) && hop.subscriber.endsWith('/strong')"
        },
        {
          "from": ".",
          "to": "./curator",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_model' && has(hop.subscriber) && hop.subscriber.endsWith('/curator/summarizer')"
        },
        {
          "from": ".",
          "to": "./memory-hive",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_model' && has(hop.subscriber) && hop.subscriber.contains('/memory-hive/')"
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": ".",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'answer' && has(hop.sa_rim) && hop.sa_rim == 'out'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_hop": {
              "route": "'answer'"
            },
            "delete_context": [
              "col_phase",
              "curator_call",
              "tool_answerer",
              "recall_input_soft",
              "input_soft",
              "gap_ask",
              "tools_folded",
              "sa_pack",
              "sa_kind",
              "pack_sub",
              "pack_hash",
              "agent_id",
              "tools_allow",
              "tools_deny",
              "tool_require",
              "ds_kind",
              "sa_stage"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": ".",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'calls' && has(hop.sa_rim) && hop.sa_rim == 'out'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_hop": {
              "route": "'calls'"
            },
            "delete_context": [
              "col_phase",
              "curator_call",
              "tool_answerer",
              "recall_input_soft",
              "input_soft",
              "gap_ask",
              "tools_folded",
              "sa_pack",
              "sa_kind",
              "pack_sub",
              "pack_hash",
              "agent_id",
              "tools_allow",
              "tools_deny",
              "tool_require",
              "ds_kind",
              "sa_stage"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": ".",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'close_report' && has(hop.sa_rim) && hop.sa_rim == 'out'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_hop": {
              "route": "'close_report'"
            },
            "delete_context": [
              "col_phase",
              "curator_call",
              "tool_answerer",
              "recall_input_soft",
              "input_soft",
              "gap_ask",
              "tools_folded",
              "sa_pack",
              "sa_kind",
              "pack_sub",
              "pack_hash",
              "agent_id",
              "tools_allow",
              "tools_deny",
              "tool_require",
              "ds_kind",
              "sa_stage"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": ".",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'error' && has(hop.sa_rim) && hop.sa_rim == 'out'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_hop": {
              "route": "'error'"
            },
            "delete_context": [
              "col_phase",
              "curator_call",
              "tool_answerer",
              "recall_input_soft",
              "input_soft",
              "gap_ask",
              "tools_folded",
              "sa_pack",
              "sa_kind",
              "pack_sub",
              "pack_hash",
              "agent_id",
              "tools_allow",
              "tools_deny",
              "tool_require",
              "ds_kind",
              "sa_stage"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": ".",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'affinity_propose' && has(hop.sa_rim) && hop.sa_rim == 'out'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_hop": {
              "route": "'affinity_propose'"
            },
            "delete_context": [
              "col_phase",
              "curator_call",
              "tool_answerer",
              "recall_input_soft",
              "input_soft",
              "gap_ask",
              "tools_folded",
              "sa_pack",
              "sa_kind",
              "pack_sub",
              "pack_hash",
              "agent_id",
              "tools_allow",
              "tools_deny",
              "tool_require",
              "ds_kind",
              "sa_stage"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": "./collector",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_turn' && !has(hop.sa_scope)",
          "modifier": {
            "set_context": {
              "session_id": "hop.session_id",
              "turn_id": "hop.turn_id",
              "iter": "'0'",
              "channel": "hop.channel",
              "audience_set": "hop.audience_set",
              "agent_id": "hop.agent_id",
              "tool_require": "has(hop.tool_require) ? hop.tool_require : ''",
              "counterpart": "has(hop.counterpart) ? hop.counterpart : ''",
              "sa_stage": "has(hop.sa_stage) ? hop.sa_stage : 'fast'"
            },
            "restore_ttl": true
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": "./collector",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_turn' && has(hop.sa_scope)",
          "modifier": {
            "set_context": {
              "session_id": "hop.session_id",
              "turn_id": "hop.turn_id",
              "iter": "'0'",
              "channel": "hop.channel",
              "audience_set": "hop.audience_set",
              "agent_id": "hop.agent_id",
              "tools_allow": "hop.tools_allow",
              "tools_deny": "hop.tools_deny",
              "tool_require": "has(hop.tool_require) ? hop.tool_require : ''",
              "counterpart": "has(hop.counterpart) ? hop.counterpart : ''",
              "sa_stage": "has(hop.sa_stage) ? hop.sa_stage : 'fast'"
            },
            "restore_ttl": true
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": "./collector",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_menu'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_context": {
              "tool_answerer": "hop.tool_answerer"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": "./collector",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_tool'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_context": {
              "session_id": "hop.session_id",
              "turn_id": "hop.turn_id",
              "iter": "hop.iter",
              "channel": "hop.channel",
              "audience_set": "hop.audience_set",
              "sa_stage": "has(hop.sa_stage) ? hop.sa_stage : 'fast'"
            },
            "restore_ttl": true
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": "./curator",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_pack'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_context": {
              "sa_pack": "'door'"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": "./collector",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'mutation_committed'"
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": "./curator",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_close'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_context": {
              "session_id": "hop.session_id",
              "channel": "hop.channel",
              "audience_set": "hop.audience_set",
              "sa_kind": "hop.sa_kind"
            },
            "restore_ttl": true
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": "./memory-hive",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'in_episode'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_context": {
              "session_id": "hop.session_id",
              "turn_id": "hop.turn_id",
              "channel": "hop.channel",
              "audience_set": "hop.audience_set",
              "happened_at": "has(hop.happened_at) ? hop.happened_at : ''"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": "./memory-hive",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'clock_op'"
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": "./watch",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'watch_op'"
        },
        {
          "from": "./door",
          "to": "./door_store",
          "condition": "has(hop.route) && hop.route == 'door_store'",
          "modifier": {
            "set_context": {
              "ds_kind": "hop.ds_kind"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./door_store",
          "to": "./door",
          "condition": "has(context.ds_kind)",
          "modifier": {
            "set_hop": {
              "route": "'door_store_ack'"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "from": "./watch",
          "to": "./collector",
          "condition": "has(hop.schedule_name) && hop.schedule_name.startsWith('round-')",
          "modifier": {
